{
  "name": "rust-postgres",
  "description": "A pure-Rust client implementation of the PostgreSQL wire protocol (v3), providing a high-level, type-safe interface for database interactions. It features native support for prepared statements, transactions with savepoints, lazy query execution for large datasets, and a built-in fixed-size connection pool. The driver enforces strict type correspondence between Rust and PostgreSQL types through extensible ToSql and FromSql traits.",
